---
import FourLawsLayout from '../layouts/FourLawsLayout.astro';

// Where the Four Laws contact form (contact.astro) posts on success — kept as
// its own page rather than merged into src/pages/thanks.astro (the main
// site's waitlist-signup thank-you), because the two forms make different
// promises: this one talks about corrections to the Full Reference, the
// main one talks about the waitlist. A single generic page would have had to
// water down whichever promise didn't apply, for a savings of one file.
//
// noindex because a confirmation page in search results is a dead end for
// whoever lands on it.
---

<FourLawsLayout
	title="Thanks"
	description="Your message has been sent."
	noindex={true}
>
	<h1>Thanks — that's sent.</h1>

	<p class="standfirst">
		I read everything that comes through here. If it needs a reply you'll get
		one; if it's a correction to the Full Reference, it'll show up in the
		document rather than in your inbox.
	</p>

	<hr class="hairline" />

	<p>
		In the meantime: the <a href="/four-laws-complex-system-design-full">Full
		Reference</a> is the whole argument in one document, and the
		<a href="/part8-flow-diagnostic">Flow &amp; Constraint Diagnostic</a> will
		tell you which of the four laws your situation is actually running into.
	</p>
</FourLawsLayout>

<style>
	.standfirst { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
